WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.133
-Thank you for being here.
-How cool. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:05.033
-Feels great, right?
Come on, yeah. They love you.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:07.033
I want to thank you
for being here,

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.701
but I will say how cool it was
to meet your sister,

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:09.601
by the way, backstage.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:10.634
-Sister's here, yeah.

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:11.934
-Caroline?
-Caroline.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:12.901
It was just her birthday.

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:14.300
-It was?
Happy birthday, Caroline.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.467
Should have said it backstage.

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:17.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:20.400
But that was a cool story that
you told me back there.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.067
I guess when you were about to
start acting,

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:24.467
she encouraged you,
and she said...?

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:28.133
-Yeah, I was probably, like,
a freshman in high school,

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.501
and she was a part of, like,
stage crew.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:31.901
You know, sound and lights.
-Yeah.

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:34.400
-And I was gonna
sleep in and skip

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.667
and just miss
the stage crew thing,

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.267
but she was like,
"Come on, get up," you know,

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:38.501
and sort of brought me along.

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:39.834
And you know, yeah.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:40.968
-Got you into the theater.
-Got me into it, yeah.

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:43.400
-And thank goodness
you stuck with it.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.934
-I did.
-Did she say, "If you do this,

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.767
and you get on 'Fallon'..."

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:47.968
-Exactly.
-"I gotta be there."

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:49.634
-I gotta be there.
-And she's here.

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.334
-And she's here tonight.
-So it's all happening.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.868
This is all supposed to happen.
-Yes.

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:55.968
-Caroline, we thank you.
-Thank you, Caroline.

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:59.734
-Steve Harrington, this is
your first big break.

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:00.968
-For sure, yeah.

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.801
-Where were you working
before then?

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:05.367
-I was a waiter.
-Good.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:06.701
-Waiter.
-You have to.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:09.033
-Have to, yeah, waiting tables
and doing commercials.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:10.267
-How were you as a waiter?

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.000
-I was a pretty good waiter,
I think.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.300
-Really?
-I was a great waiter.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:17.200
I was pretty, uh, charismatic.
-Okay, I like that.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.868
-And what I lacked in
organization,

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:23.667
I made up for in maybe,
delivery, I guess I would say.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.434
-Yeah, and you just got
the audition,

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:26.901
and you were like,

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.133
were you working when
you found out?

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:32.100
-I was, so I auditioned for,
you know,

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.934
they did the big cattle call
or whatever.

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:36.234
You know how it works, they
send out across the country.

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.868
Taped it, didn't hear anything.
Moved on.

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:42.534
3 months later, got a callback
for some different role,

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:44.234
for Steve, and I was like, "Oh,
man, the jerky boyfriend?

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:45.400
Okay, whatever."

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:48.167
And sent that in, yeah.
-That's hilarious.

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:49.334
The jerky boyfriend, yeah.
-The jerky boyfriend.

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:50.734
It was what he was.

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:52.601
It was like, you know, James
Spader in "Pretty in Pink."

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:53.834
Something like that.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:56.734
-And so my friend,
Matt Williams,

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:58.968
he would kind of help me
tape all my auditions.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:01.367
And we just, you know,
set up the camera.

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:04.601
Got, like, two mugs,
pretty DIY,

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:05.801
and did the tape, and then

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:08.033
he worked at
the restaurant with me,

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.501
and so when they did call

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:10.968
and I ended up getting
the job and stuff,

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:13.534
there was a nice moment of,
like, a silent...

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:15.734
He was a food runner
and I was a waiter,

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:19.033
and I got the call in the back,
and was like, "Oh, my God.

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:21.934
This is great. I don't have to
work at a restaurant anymore!"

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:22.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:24.267
And I saw him.

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:26.801
He was probably stocking
the truffle aioli or something.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:29.100
An I just gave him, like, a,
"I got the job!"

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.367
-Yeah! And he was like,
"What's up, buddy?"

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.067
-He was like, "Yeah!
Get back to work, though!"

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:35.200
-Get back to work, yeah.
"We'll celebrate after."

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.167
-"Is this for 9?
Are you table 9, right?"

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:41.167
-You didn't think you were gonna
make it past Season 1?

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:43.000
-Yeah, the brothers wrote,
you know --

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.234
I read one, maybe, episode
of the show, two episodes,

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:49.634
and it was kind of like,
we read three episodes

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:51.100
and then they had
two more and stuff.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.767
So it was really, they were
building it as they were going.

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:54.267
-It was day-to-day for you.
-It was day-to-day.

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:56.033
-I can't imagine
the show without you.

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:57.467
-That's very nice of you to say.

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.868
-You are "Stranger Things."
We need you. We need Steve.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:01.000
[ Cheering ]

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.901
-Thank you.
-You make the whole show.

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:04.267
I love you.

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:05.501
-Thank you.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.334
I will tell the brothers
that you said that.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.701
-Yeah, please.
They made me nervous.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.868
Because, you know,
before this season,

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:13.467
Netflix put out a billboard,

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:14.701
I don't know if saw this but...

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:16.501
-Yeah, I did see this.
-Look at this.

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:18.934
This is on the billboard.
It says "Protect Steve."

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.200
-Yeah.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.434
So I actually paid for this.
It was really expensive.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:23.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:24.834
-Wow.
-It was.

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:27.200
-Oh, that's a lot of money.
-I pretty much broke even.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.334
It was worth it.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:30.634
-It was totally worth it.
-Yeah.

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.834
-But you obviously --
we can say this.

00:03:32.834 --> 00:03:34.701
We're allowed to say it,
because...

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.667
-I'll let you say it.
-I'll do it.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:38.567
Noah came on the show
and said, someone dies.

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:40.801
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.534
-It's not you.
-It's not me.

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:43.968
-Okay. There you go.
We can say that.

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:46.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:49.968
-Are you tough with the spoilers

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.901
and holding in the secrets
and all that stuff?

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:53.033
-Um...

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:54.834
-Like your family wanted...?
-Not super.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:57.501
-Does Caroline know?

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:58.667
-Yeah, she knows.

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:00.501
Well, she doesn't --
She gets very scared.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.934
A lot of my family doesn't like
scary stuff, unfortunately.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:04.667
-Especially if it's to do
with their family member.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:05.701
Yeah, exactly.

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:07.200
-Joe? You can't, yeah.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.267
-You know, they'll watch some,
but mostly kind of through...

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:13.667
It's pretty scary.
-It's a global phenomenon.

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.133
Congratulations.
It's the biggest thing.

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:18.000
And you just got nominated
for, like, 13 Emmy Awards.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.834
-Those brothers,
it's like their life.

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:21.234
They deserve it.
They're the best.

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:23.467
-The Duffer Brothers are great.
-They're the best guys.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.200
-They are, right?
And creative and fun.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.968
But when did you realize,
like, that it is global?

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.100
It's, like, bigger than just...
It's bigger than Chicago.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.167
It's big in America.
It's bigger than.

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.934
-We did some press.

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:36.567
My other sister, Lizzie,
came with me,

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:40.868
and we went and did
some press in in Italy,

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:42.667
which was my --

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:44.601
I had gone
in high school as a trip.

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:46.067
Pretty cool high school trip,
actually.

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:47.234
To go to Italy.
I mean, that's pretty cool.

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:48.434
-Wow.

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:50.734
-That's a story
for another day.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:52.167
But we went for the press,

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:54.567
and we were kind of
walking down the street

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.934
and there was just --
we were walking,

00:04:56.934 --> 00:05:00.968
and this little Italian girl,
saw me, clocked me.

00:05:00.968 --> 00:05:02.567
I could tell.

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:03.901
And then I heard her go,

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:04.901
[ Italian accent ]
"Stranger Things!"

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:06.934
From behind. I was like...
-Wow.

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.100
-Oh, my gosh.
-In a different accent.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.367
To hear "Stranger Things."

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:10.400
[ Italian accent ]
"Stranger Things!"

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.868
-"Lizzie, let's go!"

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:14.133
-Wow.
This is actually becoming giant.

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:17.000
-Exactly, yeah, you kind of...

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.200
You know, it feels like
such a small thing when you're

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.334
doing it down there, when
you're shooting and working.

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:22.801
-And then to see
the final product.

00:05:22.801 --> 00:05:25.200
-So many people have seen it.
It's crazy.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.300
-I feel like you're also --
I've seen you perform,

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.534
as well, live as a musician.

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:31.467
-Oh.
-So you must feed off...

00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:33.033
-Do like doing it,
feeding off the audience?

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:37.534
-I mean yeah. Like, I come
from doing high school theater.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:38.834
I mean, that's what I...

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.501
-That's a good energy.
-It's a good energy.

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:42.167
It's all about that live thing.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:46.601
So when I lived in Chicago,
that was kind of my --

00:05:46.601 --> 00:05:48.167
I didn't do any theater there.

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:50.033
The name of your band,
just because

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:51.734
I think I'm saying it right.
-Yeah.

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:53.801
-It's "Joe." Is that correct?

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:56.501
-Correct. It's very confusing.

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:58.000
-Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.534
So then you walk in the room,
you go, "I'm here to see Joe."

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:01.968
Well, that's interesting,

00:06:01.968 --> 00:06:03.133
because it's spelled...

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:06.467
-D-J-O.
-Yeah.

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:07.634
-"Joe."
-It's really funny.

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:09.200
-There's not really
a story behind it.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.234
I had a bunch --
-Like DiGiorno?

00:06:10.234 --> 00:06:12.200
-Like DiGiorno, pretty much.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.167
-Yeah.
-So, not delivery, is Djo.

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:16.534
-Exactly.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:16.534 --> 00:06:19.801
-It's Djorno.
-It's Djorno.

00:06:19.801 --> 00:06:21.868
-But why "Djo"? Any reason?

00:06:21.868 --> 00:06:23.200
-Nah, I just thought --

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:27.367
I wanted to put it out
with, it's connected to me,

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:29.934
but it's not, you know,
directly connected to me,

00:06:29.934 --> 00:06:31.501
was the idea.

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:32.534
-Does it confuse people?

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:34.033
-It confuses people
all the time.

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:36.834
People say D-joe, DiGiornio.
All sorts of different --

00:06:36.834 --> 00:06:38.634
-DJ Oh! Yeah, yeah.
-DJ OH!

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:41.300
[ Imitates record scratch ]
-"I'm not a DJ. I'm a band."

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.367
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:44.601
-But you have
a new record coming out.

00:06:44.601 --> 00:06:46.367
-Yep, yep.
-September?

00:06:46.367 --> 00:06:49.033
-Yep, September 16th.
And, you know, fun.

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:50.334
-Do you know the title?
Can we say it?

00:06:50.334 --> 00:06:52.167
-We can. It's called "Decide."

00:06:52.167 --> 00:06:53.601
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:55.467
No way. So that's out September.

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:56.934
"Decide"?
-Decide, yeah.

00:06:56.934 --> 00:06:58.801
-"Decide" comes out
September 16th.

00:06:58.801 --> 00:07:01.067
-"D'just Decide," probably.
-Yeah.

00:07:01.067 --> 00:07:03.868
You always add a "D'".
You can always add that in post.

00:07:03.868 --> 00:07:05.400
-Exactly.
-You can always add that later.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.534
But you're playing big gigs.

00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:09.300
You're playing Lollapalooza?
-Man. Yeah.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.267
I'm going to be
definitely nervous.

00:07:11.267 --> 00:07:12.300
Are you excited?
-It's fun!

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:13.534
I get to wear this wig.

00:07:13.534 --> 00:07:15.868
I wear a wig and get to
dress up the whole band.

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.567
It's kind of like a Devo
sort of thing.

00:07:17.567 --> 00:07:20.234
Everyone dresses up.
-No.

00:07:20.234 --> 00:07:21.367
-Yeah.
-You do that?

00:07:21.367 --> 00:07:22.868
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, yeah.

00:07:22.868 --> 00:07:24.234
-And do people...

00:07:24.234 --> 00:07:25.868
Because then
you can walk around

00:07:25.868 --> 00:07:27.000
and go in the crowd
and not be noticed?

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.100
-Well, that was the idea.

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:31.033
I released it with
this different name.

00:07:31.033 --> 00:07:32.434
I was kind of like, you know,

00:07:32.434 --> 00:07:35.734
inspired by Andy Kaufman,
you know?

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:38.033
-Of course.
-So that was kind of the idea.

00:07:38.033 --> 00:07:40.567
Kind of this alter ego.
-I think it's great.

00:07:40.567 --> 00:07:42.267
You're fantastic.
And I think you could do it.

00:07:42.267 --> 00:07:43.767
You could do both
for a long time.

00:07:43.767 --> 00:07:45.267
-That's the idea.
Just keep doing that.

00:07:45.267 --> 00:07:47.901
And that'll kind of be fueled
by, you know, acting stuff.

00:07:47.901 --> 00:07:49.968
-Keep crushing it, buddy.
-Thank you.

00:07:49.968 --> 00:07:51.667
I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:07:51.667 --> 00:07:54.701
Here is a joke here in
Season 4 of Volume 2

00:07:54.701 --> 00:07:55.734
of "Stranger Things."

00:07:55.734 --> 00:07:56.968
Take a look at this.

00:07:56.968 --> 00:07:59.234
-I'm not sure I love the idea
of you driving.

00:07:59.234 --> 00:08:00.434
-I'm just starting the sucker.

00:08:00.434 --> 00:08:04.133
Harrington's got it.
Don't you, big boy?

00:08:04.734 --> 00:08:06.834
[ Electricity crackles ]

00:08:06.834 --> 00:08:10.300
-What the hell? Hey!
Open this door!

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.901
-Hey!

00:08:11.901 --> 00:08:15.767
-Unlock the doors!
-[Bleep]. [Bleep].

00:08:15.767 --> 00:08:17.834
-Everybody hang onto something!

00:08:17.834 --> 00:08:20.534
-Oh, my God. Oh, my God.
Let's go, let's go!

00:08:20.534 --> 00:08:23.934
-Drive, Steve, drive!
-Go, go, go!

00:08:23.934 --> 00:08:27.167
[ Screaming ]

00:08:27.167 --> 00:08:28.534
-Go, go, go!
-[Bleep].

00:08:28.534 --> 00:08:30.567
-Go, go, go!
-[Bleep]! They look pissed.

00:08:30.567 --> 00:08:32.300
-I mean, it's not
every day you lose

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:35.868
your house and car
in one fell swoop.

00:08:35.868 --> 00:08:37.534
-Hold on, hold on!

00:08:37.534 --> 00:08:41.467
♪♪

00:08:41.467 --> 00:08:43.300
-Oh, my God.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.400
-That's how you do it
right there!

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:46.033
Joe Keery, everybody!

00:08:46.033 --> 00:08:48.000
Season 4 of "Stranger Things"

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.634
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:08:49.634 --> 00:08:51.801
"Decide" comes out
September 16th.

